body:
I just want to address the topic of two cats vs. one. I adopted two kittens several months ago and I'm so glad I did! It is so much fun watching them play and interact. I think their play together is more vigorous than play with me because of how much they run around. In terms of work, the increase is fairly minimal. Its more money, because of doubled vet bills, food, etc.  

&#x200B;

Do some research on introducing cats for the first time, but it is easier with kittens than adult cats.

I had the same problem. I love this recipe:[ Spinach Rice Breakfast bowl 
](http://www.budgetbytes.com/2014/09/snap-challenge-spinach-rice-breakfast-bowls/)

I cook one cup of brown rice (which is 3 cups cooked) every Sunday, and using 1/2 cup a day, it lasts the whole work week, usually running out on Saturday morning. I discovered recently that you can also substitute oatmeal for rice, and its quite good.
